<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104012" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμάω</span>
			, in 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Schwyzer</u>
				417.5
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Elis</span>); but the Rhodian forms 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμοῦντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(1).155
				</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				 i 10
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμοῦσα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1033.12
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span> may be the contractions of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμάοντες</span>, etc., cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγλούκριτος</span> (from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγλαό-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				4245.77
			</span></i>, if not forms of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμέω</span>
			(q.v.).</div>
